type":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Fund transaction fees (charged to the AP)**\n\n- **Fixed fee:** Covers the standard costs of processing each creation or redemption order, such as transfer-agent and custodian settlement and transfer costs. It is charged per order, regardless of size.\n- **Variable fee:** Covers costs that depend on the trade, such as brokerage commissions, spreads, market impact and taxes. These arise when the fund buys or sells securities, for example with cash creations, cash substitutions or custom baskets.\n\n**Who bears them:** The authorized participant pays these fees. It typically passes them on to the customer it is transacting for. The purpose is to protect existing shareholders from dilution, consistent with Rule 6c-11.\n\n**Recipients may differ:** The variable fee usually goes to the fund to offset its trading costs. The fixed fee may instead go to the custodian or transfer agent, or to the adviser if it pays those costs.\n\n**AP compensation is separate:** APs earn arbitrage profits and may charge their own clients commissions or markups. These are not fund charges and are not paid to or by the fund.","ttft_ms":5119,"type":"result","duration_ms":8555,"uuid":"a5cf6b57-1383-4ea8-9cfb-d3f3d8c36118","ttft_stream_ms":1210,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":1211,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
